  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of workers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The 2026&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x201c;2027 period will be critical for labour governance in Indonesia, as at least three major legislative processes are expected to be concluded: the Labour Law, the Law on the Protection of Migrant Workers, and the National Social Security System (SJSN) Law. Trade union strengthening efforts will therefore focus on enabling meaningful union engagement in the formulation of these three laws, to ensure the continued safeguarding of labour standards.

Capacity-building for trade unions on freedom of association, collective bargaining, and effective social dialogue at sectoral and subnational levels will be sustained. The role of trade unions will also be expanded to address emerging and strategic issues, including energy transition, the protection of vulnerable workers, plantations, critical minerals, and platform-based work. Effective social dialogue will remain the cornerstone of stable industrial relations and the development of inclusive labour policies.</narrative>
  </description>
